# Quality gates (every task)

## Before you finish

Run lint and typecheck for every package you changed. Do not mark the task complete until both pass with **zero errors and zero warnings**.

From the **repo root** (preferred — matches CI):

```bash
pnpm lint
pnpm typecheck
```

When only one app or package changed, you may scope (faster):

```bash
pnpm app <flint|beacon|tower> lint
pnpm app <flint|beacon|tower> typecheck
# or: pnpm exec turbo run lint typecheck --filter=@codalyn/<name>
```

Beacon also supports `pnpm lint:all` (typecheck + lint in one command).

## Fixing issues

- Resolve **all** Biome diagnostics (errors and warnings), not only errors.
- Use `pnpm lint:fix` or `pnpm app <app> lint:fix` only when formatting or safe auto-fixes are intended.
- Do not add `biome-ignore` / `eslint-disable` unless unavoidable; Beacon enforces this via `scripts/assert-no-biome-ignore.mjs`.
- Do not use `@ts-expect-error`, `@ts-ignore`, or `as any` to silence type errors without a documented, narrow reason.

## If checks fail

Fix the root cause in the changed code. Do not leave the repo in a failing lint or typecheck state.
